# Mobile (Flutter) — Platform Entry & Checklist

**Platforms:** Android, iOS (do not expand legacy/frozen Flutter Web targets when a dedicated web frontend exists).

This rule binds the complete mobile engineering contract across **`#1–8`** simultaneously — never wait for separate rule mentions:

| File | Role |
| --- | --- |
| **`rules.mdc`** | Master index, priority hierarchy, and reply formatting |
| **`git-commits.mdc`** | English commits without AI/tool co-author trailers |
| **`english-comments-only.mdc`** | English-only comments; 100% l10n for UI strings |
| **`engineering-quality.mdc`** | `flutter analyze` clean, `context.mounted`, lazy controllers, Windows `;` |
| **`mandatory-design.mdc`** | Semantic context colors, `font*W*` typography, unified icons, shared widgets, bidi/l10n |
| **`interaction-ux.mdc`** | Confirmations, custom toasts, skeletons, 0ms optimistic UI, tap guards, insets |
| **`architecture-and-state.mdc`** | Feature-first folders, thin screens, Cubit/BLoC patterns, scoped rebuilds |
| **`data-sync-and-security.mdc`** | Any backend/DB abstraction, crypto isolates, authoritative sync, FCM tray hot paths |

Web app work → **`web-frontend.mdc`**. Shared database migrations → single project migrations directory.

