## Flutter Mandatory Quick Checks

- **`flutter analyze`:** Zero errors, zero warnings, zero `info` diagnostics on every change (`dart fix --apply` first for auto-fixable items).
- **Lifecycle safety:** Always check `context.mounted` (or `mounted`) after every `await` before navigation, dialogs, sheets, or toasts.
- **Colors & sizing:** Never `withOpacity()` (always `withValues(alpha:)` on `context.*`); never `.sp`/`.w`/`.h`/`.r` (ScreenUtil) on new or touched UI; never `TextStyle(height: …)` or fixed-height primary text wrappers.
- **UI exclusivity:** Never raw `ScaffoldMessenger.of(context).showSnackBar`, `TextField`, `AlertDialog`, or `CachedNetworkImage` directly in features when shared wrappers exist.
- **TabBar re-tap safety:** Track `_currentActiveTabIndex` explicitly in state; never rely on `_tabController.index` inside `TabBar.onTap` (Flutter updates `_tabController.index` before firing `onTap`).
- **Keyboard & insets:** One bottom inset owner per screen/composer; dismiss keyboard cleanly before async submit/navigation.

