## Crashlytics & Native Error Reporting Checklist

| Cause | Solution |
| --- | --- |
| Running in **Debug** mode (`flutter run`) | Crashlytics is disabled by default in `kDebugMode`. Test with `flutter run --release` or `--dart-define=ENABLE_CRASHLYTICS_IN_DEBUG=true` |
| Expecting instantaneous crash reports | Fatal crashes upload on the **next app launch** after the crash occurs |
| Test crash call in startup path | Never call `FirebaseCrashlytics.instance.crash()` during app initialization — it breaks the launch cycle |
| Crashlytics not enabled in Firebase | Firebase Console → target project → Crashlytics → Get started |
| Android application/bundle ID mismatch | Ensure `applicationId` matches `google-services.json` (`package_name`) |
| iOS missing dSYM symbols | Add Run Script Phase in Xcode to upload dSYMs via FlutterFire CLI or Firebase script |
| ProGuard / R8 stripping symbols | Keep `-keep class com.google.firebase.crashlytics.** { *; }` / `crashlytics.**` in `proguard-rules.pro` |
